      "text_runs": [
        "The idea of dominant and recessive alleles was first described by Gregor Mendel…",
        "He conducted test crosses with peas of different phenotypes and r",
        "ealized that for each trait, offspring displayed ",
        "either the maternal or paternal phenotype ",
        "rather than a blending of the two.",
        "E.g. a ",
        "true-breeding ",
        "(",
        "i.e. homozygous)",
        " plant with purple flowers crossed with a ",
        "true-breeding ",
        "(i.e. ",
        "homozygous)",
        " ",
        "plant with white flowers always produced offspring with purple flowers, not light purple as previously suggested by the blending theory of inheritance",
        "Thus, he concluded that purple flowers were dominant to white",
        "Mendelian Genetics"
      ],
      "images": [
        {
          "Id": "rId3",
          "Type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image",
